{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1786972851,"nonce":"U52Y2cTTlaA6/6zS4CrCTXKXP0U=","message":"Landed in `bfa3f9d`.\n\n`PageEmptyState` in `states.tsx` is the distinct full-page component the ticket asked for, not a prop on the shared one. The shared `EmptyState` is untouched, so one quiet alert still renders six plain sub-panels — and `Ink.test.tsx` reads `features/alerts/detail/` off disk to keep it that way, so a seventh sub-panel added later is covered by the gate rather than by somebody remembering.\n\nKumo on the quiet states, sakura on `expired`, one motif per state, never both — the motif is a required single prop, so \"both\" is not expressible. Every motif is `aria-hidden`, static, and each state still reads correctly with the ink removed.\n\n**Clear of the text, structurally.** The ticket asked for corner-anchored and never touching the text; that is enforced the same way the door's is, with `clearColumn(\"28rem\")` intersected with the art against a sentence capped at `max-w-96`. The ink is geometrically excluded at every viewport width, and on a narrow one it disappears rather than sliding under the words.\n\n**The `expired` empty state had to be invented, because it did not exist.** There was no screen whose emptiness was *about* expiry — filtering the list to `expired` and getting nothing produced \"No alerts match these filters\", which is exactly the conflation this ticket describes. `isExpiredOnly()` (state is exactly `[expired]`, everything else at its default) now tells the two apart and the state gets its own sentence: \"Nothing has gone quiet.\" The petal is the second channel beside it (U1), never the carrier.\n\n**One call site on the list deliberately did not get a motif: `alerts.tsx:487`, the blocked filter.** Kumo means stillness — nothing is wrong, and that is the point. There something *is* wrong and there is a fix two lines below it, so a serene cloud would be the ink saying the opposite of the sentence. The reason is written at the call site rather than left as an omission.\n\nThe other five are done: `alerts.tsx` roll-up-empty and both list-empty branches, `groups.tsx:229`, `PoliciesSection.tsx:310`. The `states.tsx` \"only decorative art in the app\" comment is amended rather than deleted, and says what is still true of it.\n\nThe sakura asset is rotated 28° inside its own box, which is not decoration: drawn upright, a notched petal and a heart are the same outline and only the angle tells them apart. That was only visible by rendering it.\n\n`/proto/ui-preview` now has an ink band with both motifs and both heading shapes in it, in either theme, with no backend — because a mask that letterboxes itself into invisibility is the one failure no unit test in this repository can see.","files":null}]}